From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: the UI Automation to MSAA bridge

UiaReturnRawElementProvider answered only UiaRootObjectId; for OBJID_CLIENT
it returned nothing (a FIXME), so a program with a UI Automation provider
was invisible to MSAA clients (screen readers and oleacc's users). As
documented for the bridge, OBJID_CLIENT now gets an IAccessible made from
the provider (dlls/uiautomationcore/uia_bridge.c):

- get_accName (Name), get_accHelp (HelpText), get_accKeyboardShortcut
  (AccessKey, else AcceleratorKey), get_accDescription (FullDescription,
  else ItemStatus), get_accValue (the Value or RangeValue pattern) and
  put_accValue (IValueProvider::SetValue);
- get_accRole from the control type; get_accState from IsEnabled,
  IsKeyboardFocusable, HasKeyboardFocus, IsOffscreen, IsPassword and the
  Toggle, SelectionItem, ExpandCollapse and Value patterns;
- children, accNavigate (first/last child, next/previous) and
  get_accParent from fragment navigation (the root's parent is its
  window's OBJID_WINDOW object); accLocation from BoundingRectangle;
  accHitTest from the fragment root's ElementProviderFromPoint;
  get_accFocus from HasKeyboardFocus and the root's GetFocus;
  get_accSelection from the Selection pattern (one object, or an
  IEnumVARIANT of several);
- get_accDefaultAction and accDoDefaultAction: Invoke, Toggle,
  ExpandCollapse or SelectionItem; accSelect: SetFocus and the selection
  item's Select/AddToSelection/RemoveFromSelection;
- IServiceProvider gives back the provider (IID_IRawElementProviderSimple),
  which UIA_PFIA_UNWRAP_BRIDGE (1683) uses; IOleWindow gives the window.

The provider map call (all arguments zero) has nothing to free: the
bridge's objects hold their providers.

Gate: test/uiabridge-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, a client in another process,
test/uiabridge-probe.c). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_BRIDGE, SG_MUTANT_NO_BRIDGE_ACTION
(uia_bridge.c).
---
--- a/dlls/uiautomationcore/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/uiautomationcore/Makefile.in
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ SOURCES = \
 	uia_classes.idl \
 	uia_classes_client.idl \
 	uia_classes_core.idl \
+	uia_bridge.c \
 	uia_client.c \
 	uia_com_client.c \
 	uia_event.c \
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/uiautomationcore/uia_bridge.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1038 @@
+/*
+ * The UI Automation to MSAA bridge (Stained Glass OS 1685)
+ *
+ * A window that answers WM_GETOBJECT with UiaReturnRawElementProvider for
+ * any object id gets, for OBJID_CLIENT, an IAccessible made from its UI
+ * Automation provider, so MSAA clients (screen readers, oleacc's own
+ * users) see it: names, roles, states, values, locations, children, focus,
+ * selection, hit testing and default actions come from the provider's
+ * properties and patterns, as documented for the bridge.
+ *
